  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Release candidate exposing the raw transaction response body for fiscal audit.\n\nHighlights:\n- TxResponse.RawJson carries the exact body a transaction response was deserialized from, so a German fiscal\n  signature can be shown to an auditor as the provider returned it rather than as this SDK read it\n- captured on both the write and the read path, so a recovery that re-observes a finished transaction with GET\n  rather than FINISH records the body too - the case an audit is most likely to ask about\n- added through new executor methods, so ExecutePutAsync/ExecuteGetAsync, every existing caller and\n  ITransactionClient keep their shape - no consumer has to change and no mock has to be retaught\n- buffering is confined to transactions; export downloads keep streaming straight into the deserializer\n- provider errors are not captured: the error handler raises before the body is read",
